{"t": 1794106390.9400358, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_add_issue_comment", "args": {"body": "\u26a0\ufe0f This change caused a production error: [LEDGER-WORKER-9A](https://acme.sentry.io/issues/LEDGER-WORKER-9A/)\n\n**ReconciliationMismatch: converted totals off by 1 minor unit** (expected 1100, got 1099) \u2014 2,201 events since release ledger-worker@2026.11.3.\n\n`int(amount_minor * rate)` truncates toward zero, so any FX result that lands just below a whole minor unit (e.g. 1099.9999 due to float representation) silently loses one minor unit and breaks reconciliation.\n\nFix: restore rounding to the nearest minor unit in `worker/rates.py` (reverting the `round(...)` -> `int(...)` change from commit 8c2f1d0).", "issue_number": 412, "owner": "acme", "repo": "ledger-worker"}, "ok": true}
